            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0754" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v06/pg719"/>

                <head>249. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                        (Tarnoff) to the President’s
                    Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d249-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-12-31">December 31, 1979</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>
                        U.S. Soviet Relations and Afghanistan</item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with the NSC request, I attach the
                    Department’s papers on U.S. Soviet relations and
                    Afghanistan for Wednesday’s<anchor n="2" xml:id="d249-f2"/>
                    NSC meeting.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#bold">
                        Peter Tarnoff
                    </hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d249-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#right">Executive Secretary</p>
                <p>Attachments:</p>
                <p>Tab 1—Afghanistan: Steps in the Framework of U.S.
                    Soviet Relations.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d249-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Tab 2—Possible U.S. Actions.</p>
                <p>Tab 3—Possible Soviet Reactions.</p>



                <xi:include href="d249-a1.xml" xpointer="d249-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Office of the Secretariat Staff, Special Adviser to
                    the Secretary (S/MS) on Soviet Affairs
                        Marshall Shulman—Jan 21, 77–Jan 19,
                    81, Lot 81D109, Box 17, Afghan-US Steps. Secret; Nodis. Cleared by Paul Kreisberg (S/P), Jerome Kahan (PM), and
                    McCall.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d249-f2" n="2" xml:id="d249-f2-content">
                <p>January 2, 1980.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d249-f3" n="3" xml:id="d249-f3-content">
                <p>
                    Bremer signed for Tarnoff above Tarnoff’s typed signature.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d249-f4" n="4" xml:id="d249-f4-content">
                <p>Tabs 1 and 3 are attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
